A||N||7||FieroFanaticus2||Oxygen Sensor Question||||1||
Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||08-26-2001||01:54 AM||||Well, I got a code 24, the oxygen sensor is acting up now.  Am Just wondering if that might be the cause of the problem I discribed earlier in this thread <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013098.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013098.html</A> <P>Does the O2 sensor have a role in how the engine idles?  would a faulty sensor possibly cause the engine to kill when the clutch is pushed in?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||08-26-2001||02:04 AM||||The O2 sensor can cause a myriad of problems, including the idle.  At this point you need to replace it anyways, so do that and see what happens.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||08-26-2001||02:07 AM||||The O2 sensor has an effect on the way the enge runs at all RPMs.  I doubt it has anything to do with the clutch being pushed in.... You most likely found your problem though.  Get a new one...it will only make things better.||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||08-26-2001||04:26 AM||||If your O2 sensor fails you'll more likely see the idle speed rythmically bounce up and down 200-300 RPM every 1-2 seconds when the engine has warmed up.  Be sure to replace the sensor with one of the good ones like a Delco, avoid the el cheapo ones. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroFanaticus2||08-26-2001||10:13 AM||||What about the one made by BOSCH?  AutoZone sells that kind.  Is that considered el Cheapo?<P>Also, I found this interesting....<BR>When I replaced my EGR Valve, I looked up the part number on the internet at autozones website.  I live between 2 autozones.  At one autozone the price was $59, and at the other id was $37.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||08-26-2001||10:31 AM||||24 is the speed sensor. 44 is O2 sensor. was that a typo?<P>Bosch is a good brand. They probably make the ones for GM.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||08-26-2001||07:43 PM||||Consider that Bosch is usually credited with inventing the O2 sensor.... I think they know what they are doing. Bosch is the only non OE brand I'll use for this sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroFanaticus2||08-26-2001||10:07 PM||||I bought the Bosch and put it in.  Everything runs great now.  I've spent about $160 changing sensors and the like, to find it was only a $20 part.  Oh well, at least it has a lot of new sensors now...<P>TPS<BR>IAC<BR>MAP<BR>EGR <BR>and finally....<BR>The O2 Sensor<P>I'm a little bugged at myself though, for most of those sensors I went to an Autozone that charges a hell of a lot more than another auto zone about the same distance just in the other direction.  The O2 sensor was $32 at one of them, I got it for $19 and some odd cents.  The EGR was $59 at the expensive AutoZone, I got it for $37 at the other one.  At least now I know where to go for parts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
